{"id": "f54dbc26-dc12-40c9-8661-360c1b9b1891", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Let me check into that lifecycle policy for you — this requires pulling the policy, simulating what it would expire, and cross-referencing against what your Batch jobs and EC2 hosts are actually using (including recorded pulls and CloudTrail activity), so I'll run that analysis now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_yPdHemxbqJEbQQJNG1gSCe", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether the ECR lifecycle policy currently attached to the repository 'nebula-batch-worker' is safe to leave as-is, following the ecr-lifecycle-guard skill's full methodology exactly.",
  "context": "User runs AWS Batch jobs on EC2 that pull container images directly from the 'nebula-batch-worker' ECR repository. They want to know if any image still in use (recorded pulls, Batch ACTIVE job definitions, or direct EC2 pulls) is at risk of being deleted by the current lifecycle policy. IMPORTANT: First call skill_read on the skill named 'ecr-lifecycle-guard' to load its full instructions, verdict model, check matrix, and report template, and follow that procedure exactly (Steps 1-9), including: GetLifecyclePolicy + DescribeImages for all images, StartLifecyclePolicyPreview (poll GetLifecyclePolicyPreview) as the authoritative expiring set with fallback simulation only if preview fails, the full in-use inventory (lastRecordedPullTime, ECS, Batch ACTIVE job definitions -- this is critical since jobs run on Batch/EC2 -- Lambda, App Runner, EKS presence, and optionally CloudTrail BatchGetImage/GetDownloadUrlForLayer/PutImage events with push-correlation filtering), and render the exact report format mandated by that skill's Output Contract (Scope, Repository Rating, Source of Truth, Expiring Images, Rule by Rule, Findings, Suggested Protective Rule, Check Matrix, Not Assessed, Next Steps) verbatim. This is a read-only control-plane review -- do not modify or delete anything, and if StartLifecyclePolicyPreview is flagged as a mutating action needing approval, note that but do not block -- fall back to simulation if not approved.",
  "resources": ["ECR repository: nebula-batch-worker", "AWS Batch (EC2 job queue/compute environment using this repo)"],
  "timeframe": "Default 30-day pull recency window per the skill (current time 2026-11-05T15:24:24Z)",
  "criteria": "Follow the ecr-lifecycle-guard skill's verdict model and check matrix precisely. Must explicitly check AWS Batch ACTIVE job definitions referencing this repository's images as an in-use source, since the user's workloads run on Batch/EC2. Return the full structured report exactly as the skill's Output Contract mandates -- do not summarize or shorten it; I will relay it verbatim to the user."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Analyze ECR lifecycle policy risk for the nebula-batch-worker repository."}], "created_at": null}
